# Implementation plan

We do this in six passes. After each one, we look at the page before starting the next.

The warm paper background and the clay accent stay. So does Manrope for reading text. The photographs stay the ones already on the site.

## 1. Make the words readable — done

Body text is a normal reading size. Captions, questions, and city names came up with it. Headlines are sentence case. The name uses its own typeface, Bodoni Moda. Everything else stays in Manrope.

Layout, pictures, and buttons were left where they were.

## 2. Take off the extra decoration — done

Each section loses the small label above the title. The spark icons, the rings on Mara’s photo, the circles behind the name, and the giant MARA watermark come out.

Arrow buttons stay only on the booking link. The ticker runs once, in a color light enough to read. The second ticker goes away. “Know More” goes away.

## 3. Show each picture once, in three stories — done

Each photo gets one spot. The work splits into Portraits, Weddings, and Brand. Frames that show another brand’s name come out.

“View Project” stops being a dead link. The side-to-side sliders go away.

## 4. Open on a photograph — done

The first thing on the page becomes one large photograph, with the name set on it. The three stories begin underneath. The share preview uses that opening photograph.

## 5. One way to book — done

Every booking button becomes “Book a session.” It opens a short note (name, email, kind of session, date) that starts an email to the studio. The shop links and the f / x / in buttons come out until those pages exist.

## 6. Put each quote with the work it describes — done

Stars, the “148” count, and the social buttons on each review come out. Wedding quotes sit with Weddings. Brand quotes sit with Brand.
